==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*sebun}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*septḿ̥}}.
Cognate with {{cog|goh|sibun}} ({{cog|de|sieben}}), {{cog|osx|siƀun}}, {{cog|nl|zeven}}, {{cog|non|sjau}} ({{cog|sv|sju}}), {{cog|got|𐍃𐌹𐌱𐌿𐌽}}; and, outside the Germanic languages, with {{cog|sa|सप्तन्|tr=saptán}}, Ancient Greek [[ἑπτά]], Latin [[septem]] (see there for further descendants), Albanian [[shtatë]], Old Irish [[secht]] (Irish [[seacht]]), Old Church Slavonic [[сєдмь]].

